# Build context for the Dockerfile.
#
# The context is what the build stage compiles and the images carry: the main module's go.mod,
# go.sum, build.sh and notices.sh, the packages the two commands build from (cmd/, internal/) and
# the nested modules go.mod replaces them with (objfile/, reader/), plus LICENSE and NOTICE for
# /licenses/. Nothing else from the repository: not docs/ (its media and evidence archives),
# bench/, testdata/, site/, tools/, scripts/ or .git. Inside the directories it admits it leaves
# out what a working tree accumulates and the build never reads: built binaries, listing output
# (Parquet parts, dataset data/ directories, run.json and error.json, checkpoints and the
# lister's .swath/ state), databases, logs, caches, editor and OS files, and private or agent
# working material. The rules mirror the repository .gitignore.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!build.sh
!notices.sh
!cmd/
!internal/
!objfile/
!reader/
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# Built binaries (build.sh -o swath, swath-<os>-<arch>, swath-replay, swath-replay-<os>-<arch>)
swath
swath-*
swath.exe
**/bin/
**/out/
**/build/

# Listing output, checkpoints and databases
**/*.parquet
**/data/part-*.parquet
**/.swath/
**/.swath-checkpoint/
**/run.json
**/error.json
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/tmp-fixtures/

# Logs, caches, editor and OS files
**/*.log
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.iml
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Private and agent working material
**/private/
**/.agent/
